WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.680
Employers see plenty of claims about AI engineers and very little proof. This directory puts the proof first.

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:17.880
A person appears here only once a case study about work they built is approved and published. No case study, no listing.

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:28.300
Inside a profile the same rule holds. A project without a published case study, and the commits from its repository, never leave the server.

4
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:37.960
With booking off, an employer asks for an introduction and the Colaberry team makes it. Candidates' contact details are never shown.

5
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:51.690
With booking on, the page offers only open times in the candidate's zone. Each request is decided under a lock, then waits for the candidate to accept, suggest another time or decline.

6
00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:03.540
Candidates can record an intro video in the browser. The coach measures pace, filler words and voice against published targets, and the face is not analysed.

7
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:17.480
Six of six listed engineers have a published case study behind them. Twenty of twenty eight modules have a test file of their own name. All sixteen commits name an AI coding assistant as co-author.

8
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:29.010
Before a fix on fourteen November most visits to the site landed in a catch-all category, and today none do. No listed engineer has switched booking on yet.

9
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:38.130
No interview has been booked, so whether a listing leads to a hire is still unmeasured. The record says so plainly.

10
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:47.580
The directory cannot list anyone without a published case study, and an employer's request waits for the candidate to decide.
